      "headline": "Birth of Allen Ginsberg",
      "text": "Irwin Allen Ginsberg was born on June 3, 1926, in Newark, New Jersey, United States.",
      "date": "1926-06-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Enrollment at Columbia University",
      "text": "In 1943, Ginsberg enrolled at Columbia University, where he met Lucien Carr, William S. Burroughs, and Jack Kerouac, forming the core of the Beat Generation.",
      "date": "1943"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Howl'",
      "text": "In 1956, Ginsberg's poem 'Howl' was published by City Lights Bookstore. The poem became famous for its explicit language and critique of modern society.",
      "date": "1956"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Obscenity Trial",
      "text": "In 1957, the poem 'Howl' was subject to an obscenity trial in San Francisco. The trial concluded with a ruling that the poem was of 'redeeming social importance'.",
      "date": "1957"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Kaddish and Other Poems'",
      "text": "In 1961, Ginsberg published 'Kaddish and Other Poems', which included the poem 'Kaddish', written in memory of his mother.",
      "date": "1961"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Involvement in the Counterculture Movement",
      "text": "Throughout the 1960s, Ginsberg became a prominent figure in the counterculture movement, advocating for free speech, gay rights, and opposition to the Vietnam War.",
      "date": "1960s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Co-founding Naropa University's Jack Kerouac School of Disembodied Poetics",
      "text": "In 1974, Ginsberg co-founded the Jack Kerouac School of Disembodied Poetics at Naropa University in Boulder, Colorado.",
      "date": "1974"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Collected Poems 1947–1980'",
      "text": "In 1984, Ginsberg published 'Collected Poems 1947–1980', a comprehensive collection of his work.",
      "date": "1984"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Allen Ginsberg",
      "text": "Allen Ginsberg died on April 5, 1997, in New York City, New York, United States, from liver cancer.",
      "date": "1997-04-05"
    }
  ]
}

