      "headline": "Introduction of Panchayati Raj System",
      "text": "In 1978, the West Bengal Legislative Assembly passed legislation to introduce the Panchayati Raj system, which decentralized power to local government bodies in rural areas.",
      "date": "1978"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Left Front Government Era",
      "text": "The Left Front, a coalition of leftist parties led by the Communist Party of India (Marxist), came to power in 1977 and ruled the state for 34 years until 2011, making it one of the longest-serving democratically elected communist governments in the world.",
      "date": "1977"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trinamool Congress Victory",
      "text": "In 2011, the All India Trinamool Congress, led by Mamata Banerjee, won the state elections, ending the 34-year rule of the Left Front. This marked a significant political shift in the state's governance.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bicameral to Unicameral Transition",
      "text": "The West Bengal Legislative Assembly was initially part of a bicameral legislature with a Legislative Council. However, the Legislative Council was abolished in 1969, making the Assembly unicameral.",
      "date": "1969"
    }
  ]
}

