      "text": "In the 1960s and 1970s, the New Wave science fiction movement emerged, with writers like Philip K. Dick, Michael Moorcock, Roger Zelazny, John Brunner, J. G. Ballard, Philip José Farmer, and Harlan Ellison. This movement examined the impact of technology, drug culture, and the sexual revolution, setting the stage for the cyberpunk genre.",
