    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Neuromancer'",
      "text": "In 1984, William Gibson published 'Neuromancer', a novel that became a cornerstone of the cyberpunk genre. It introduced concepts like cyberspace and the matrix, influencing the genre's aesthetic and themes.",
      "date": "1984"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Akira'",
      "text": "In 1988, the Japanese animated film 'Akira', directed by Katsuhiro Otomo, was released. It became a landmark in the cyberpunk genre, known for its depiction of a dystopian future and its influence on both Western and Eastern cyberpunk works.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'The Matrix'",
      "text": "In 1999, the film 'The Matrix', directed by the Wachowskis, was released. It became a cultural phenomenon and a defining work of cyberpunk cinema, exploring themes of virtual reality and artificial intelligence.",
      "date": "1999"
    },
    {
