      "headline": "Black Star Line Launch",
      "text": "In 1919, Garvey launched the Black Star Line, a shipping company intended to facilitate the transportation of goods and eventually African Americans throughout the African global economy.",
      "date": "1919"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conviction for Mail Fraud",
      "text": "In 1923, Garvey was convicted of mail fraud in connection with the Black Star Line and sentenced to five years in prison.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Deportation to Jamaica",
      "text": "After serving part of his sentence, Garvey was deported to Jamaica in 1927.",
      "date": "1927"
    },
    {
