    },
    {
      "headline": "Oslo II Accord Signed",
      "text": "On September 28, 1995, the Oslo II Accord was signed in Taba, Egypt. This agreement expanded on the Oslo I Accord, providing for Palestinian self-rule in parts of the West Bank and Gaza Strip.",
      "date": "1995-09-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Implementation of Oslo II",
      "text": "Following the signing of the Oslo II Accord, the West Bank was divided into Areas A, B, and C, with varying degrees of Palestinian and Israeli control, as part of the interim self-government arrangements.",
