      "headline": "Foundation of the Church of the East",
      "text": "The Church of the East was established in the early centuries of Christianity, traditionally attributed to the missionary efforts of the apostles Thomas, Addai, and Mari. It became distinct from other Christian communities by the 3rd century.",
      "date": "0200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Council of Seleucia-Ctesiphon",
      "text": "In 410, the Council of Seleucia-Ctesiphon was convened, which organized the Church of the East and established its independence from the Roman Church.",
      "date": "0410"
