      "text": "On October 29, 1969, the first message was sent over the ARPANET, the precursor to the Internet, from UCLA to the Stanford Research Institute.",
      "date": "1969-10-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of TCP/IP",
      "text": "In 1973, Vint Cerf and Bob Kahn introduced the Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) and Internet Protocol (IP), which became the foundational protocols for the Internet.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First International ARPANET Connection",
      "text": "In 1973, the first international ARPANET connections were made to the University College of London in England and the Royal Radar Establishment in Norway.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Email Invented",
      "text": "In 1971, Ray Tomlinson sent the first network email, using the @ symbol to separate the user's name from the computer name.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
