      "text": "In 1983, the Domain Name System (DNS) was introduced, allowing users to access websites using domain names instead of numerical IP addresses.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "ARPANET Decommissioned",
      "text": "In 1990, ARPANET was officially decommissioned, marking the end of the original network that led to the development of the Internet.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World Wide Web Launched",
      "text": "In 1991, Tim Berners-Lee launched the World Wide Web, a system of interlinked hypertext documents accessed via the Internet.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Web Browser Released",
      "text": "In 1993, the Mosaic web browser was released, making the World Wide Web more accessible to the general public.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Commercialization of the Internet",
      "text": "In 1995, the Internet was fully commercialized, with the removal of the last restrictions on carrying commercial traffic.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Google Founded",
      "text": "In 1998, Google was founded by Larry Page and Sergey Brin, eventually becoming the world's most popular search engine.",
      "date": "1998"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Social Media",
      "text": "In 2004, Facebook was launched, marking the beginning of the widespread adoption of social media platforms.",
      "date": "2004"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the iPhone",
