      "headline": "Creation of AMBER Alert",
      "text": "The AMBER Alert system was created in 1996 in the United States after the abduction and murder of Amber Hagerman, a nine-year-old girl in Arlington, Texas.",
      "date": "1996"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First AMBER Alert issued",
      "text": "The first AMBER Alert was issued in 1996 in the Dallas-Fort Worth area of Texas, shortly after the system was created.",
      "date": "1996"
    },
    {
      "headline": "National AMBER Alert Network Act",
      "text": "In 2003, the National AMBER Alert Network Act was signed into law by President George W. Bush, establishing a national AMBER Alert system.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
    {
      "headline": "AMBER Alert goes international",
      "text": "In 2004, the AMBER Alert system began to be adopted internationally, with Canada implementing its own version of the system.",
      "date": "2004"
    },
    {
      "headline": "AMBER Alert reaches all 50 states",
      "text": "By 2005, all 50 states in the United States had implemented the AMBER Alert system.",
      "date": "2005"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion to wireless alerts",
      "text": "In 2012, the AMBER Alert system expanded to include wireless emergency alerts, allowing notifications to be sent directly to mobile devices.",
      "date": "2012"
    }
  ]
}

