      "headline": "Establishment of the Bronze Star Medal",
      "text": "The Bronze Star Medal was established by Executive Order 9419 on February 4, 1944, by President Franklin D. Roosevelt. It was created to recognize heroic or meritorious achievement or service in a combat zone.",
      "date": "1944-02-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Award of the Bronze Star Medal",
      "text": "The first Bronze Star Medal was awarded during World War II. It was given retroactively to service members who had distinguished themselves in combat.",
      "date": "1944"
