      "text": "The construction and decoration of the Ajanta Caves were completed around 480 CE. This period saw the creation of some of the most intricate and expressive artworks in the caves.",
      "date": "0480"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rediscovery of Ajanta Caves",
      "text": "The Ajanta Caves were rediscovered by a British officer, John Smith, in 1819 while on a hunting expedition. This event brought the caves to the attention of the wider world.",
      "date": "1819"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Designation as UNESCO World Heritage Site",
      "text": "In 1983, the Ajanta Caves were designated as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, recognizing their significance as masterpieces of Buddhist religious art.",
      "date": "1983"
    }
  ]
}

