      "headline": "Operation Valkyrie Modified",
      "text": "In 1944, the conspirators modified Operation Valkyrie, a plan originally intended to maintain order in the event of civil unrest, to facilitate their coup after Hitler's assassination.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Assassination Attempt on Adolf Hitler",
      "text": "On 20 July 1944, Claus von Stauffenberg placed a bomb in a briefcase under a table in a conference room at the Wolf's Lair, Hitler's headquarters in East Prussia. The bomb exploded, but Hitler survived with minor injuries.",
      "date": "1944-07-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Failure of the Coup",
      "text": "Following the failed assassination attempt, the planned coup d'état was not successfully executed. The conspirators were unable to seize control of key government and military positions.",
      "date": "1944-07-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrest and Execution of Conspirators",
      "text": "In the aftermath of the failed plot, many of the conspirators, including Claus von Stauffenberg, were arrested and executed. A widespread purge of the Wehrmacht followed, targeting those suspected of involvement in the conspiracy.",
      "date": "1944-07-21"
    }
  ]
}

