      "text": "The Cali Cartel was formed in the early 1970s by the Rodríguez Orejuela brothers, Gilberto and Miguel, along with José Santacruz Londoño. Initially involved in marijuana trafficking, they later expanded into cocaine.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion into Cocaine Trafficking",
      "text": "During the late 1970s and early 1980s, the Cali Cartel expanded its operations into cocaine trafficking, establishing a significant presence in the international drug trade.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Break from Medellín Cartel",
      "text": "In 1988, the Cali Cartel broke away from Pablo Escobar and the Medellín Cartel, establishing itself as a separate and rival organization.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Four-Man Executive Board",
      "text": "In 1988, Hélmer 'Pacho' Herrera joined the Cali Cartel, forming a four-man executive board with the Rodríguez Orejuela brothers and José Santacruz Londoño to run the cartel.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peak of Power and Influence",
      "text": "By the early 1990s, the Cali Cartel had become one of the most powerful drug trafficking organizations in the world, controlling 80% of the global cocaine market.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrest of Gilberto Rodríguez Orejuela",
      "text": "On June 9, 1995, Gilberto Rodríguez Orejuela was arrested by Colombian authorities, marking the beginning of the downfall of the Cali Cartel.",
      "date": "1995-06-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrest of Miguel Rodríguez Orejuela",
      "text": "Miguel Rodríguez Orejuela was arrested on August 6, 1995, further weakening the leadership of the Cali Cartel.",
      "date": "1995-08-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of José Santacruz Londoño",
      "text": "José Santacruz Londoño was killed by Colombian police on March 5, 1996, after escaping from prison, dealing another blow to the Cali Cartel.",
      "date": "1996-03-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capture of Hélmer 'Pacho' Herrera",
      "text": "Hélmer 'Pacho' Herrera surrendered to Colombian authorities on September 1, 1996, effectively ending the leadership of the Cali Cartel.",
      "date": "1996-09-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Cali Cartel",
      "text": "By the late 1990s, with the arrest or death of its key leaders, the Cali Cartel was dismantled by Colombian and U.S. authorities.",
      "date": "1999"
    }
  ]
}

