      "headline": "Adoption in the French Revolution",
      "text": "During the French Revolution in the late 18th century, the Phrygian cap was adopted as a symbol of freedom and the pursuit of liberty, becoming an emblem of the revolutionaries.",
      "date": "1789"
    },
