      "headline": "Raleigh Founded",
      "text": "Raleigh was officially established as the capital of North Carolina in 1792. It was one of the few cities in the United States that was specifically planned and built to serve as a state capital.",
      "date": "1792"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Raleigh Incorporated",
      "text": "Raleigh was incorporated as a city in 1794, two years after its establishment as the state capital.",
      "date": "1794"
    },
    {
      "headline": "North Carolina State Capitol Completed",
      "text": "The North Carolina State Capitol building was completed in 1840. It is a National Historic Landmark and one of the best-preserved examples of a major civic building in the Greek Revival style.",
      "date": "1840"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Raleigh and Gaston Railroad",
      "text": "The Raleigh and Gaston Railroad, one of the earliest railroads in North Carolina, was completed in 1840, connecting Raleigh to the town of Gaston.",
      "date": "1840"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Raleigh During the Civil War",
      "text": "Raleigh was occupied by Union forces in April 1865 during the American Civil War. The city was spared from destruction, unlike many other Southern cities.",
      "date": "1865-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of North Carolina State University",
      "text": "North Carolina State University was founded in Raleigh in 1887 as a land-grant college focused on agriculture and engineering.",
      "date": "1887"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Raleigh's First Skyscraper",
      "text": "The Sir Walter Raleigh Hotel, which opened in 1924, was Raleigh's first skyscraper and became a social hub for the city.",
      "date": "1924"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Research Triangle Park Established",
      "text": "In 1959, Research Triangle Park was established near Raleigh, becoming one of the largest research parks in the world and significantly contributing to the region's economic growth.",
      "date": "1959"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Raleigh's Population Growth",
      "text": "By the 2020 census, Raleigh's population had grown to 467,665, making it one of the fastest-growing cities in the United States.",
      "date": "2020"
