    },
    {
      "headline": "EBU's Role in Digital Television",
      "text": "In the 1990s, the EBU played a significant role in the development and implementation of digital television standards in Europe.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eurovision Young Musicians Competition",
      "text": "The Eurovision Young Musicians competition, organized by the EBU, was first held in 1982. It is a biennial competition for young classical musicians.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
    {
      "headline": "EBU's Involvement in High-Definition Television",
      "text": "In the early 2000s, the EBU was actively involved in the promotion and development of high-definition television (HDTV) standards.",
      "date": "2000"
