      "headline": "Foundation of Bogotá",
      "text": "On August 6, 1538, Spanish conquistador Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada founded the city of Bogotá, originally named Santa Fe de Bogotá, on the site of the former Muisca village of Bacatá.",
      "date": "1538-08-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bogotá becomes the capital of the New Kingdom of Granada",
      "text": "In 1549, Bogotá was designated as the capital of the New Kingdom of Granada, a Spanish colonial territory that included much of present-day Colombia.",
      "date": "1549"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Royal Audiencia",
      "text": "In 1550, the Royal Audiencia of Bogotá was established, making the city an important administrative center in the Spanish Empire.",
      "date": "1550"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the Viceroyalty of New Granada",
      "text": "In 1717, the Viceroyalty of New Granada was created, with Bogotá as its capital, further solidifying its importance in the region.",
      "date": "1717"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence from Spain",
      "text": "On July 20, 1810, Bogotá played a central role in the independence movement against Spanish rule, marking the beginning of Colombia's struggle for independence.",
      "date": "1810-07-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Boyacá",
      "text": "On August 7, 1819, the Battle of Boyacá took place near Bogotá, leading to a decisive victory for the independence forces and the eventual liberation of New Granada from Spanish control.",
      "date": "1819-08-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bogotá becomes the capital of Gran Colombia",
      "text": "In 1821, after the independence of New Granada, Bogotá became the capital of the newly formed nation of Gran Colombia.",
      "date": "1821"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bogotá as the capital of the Republic of Colombia",
      "text": "Following the dissolution of Gran Colombia in 1831, Bogotá became the capital of the Republic of Colombia.",
      "date": "1831"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bogotá's name change to Santa Fe de Bogotá",
      "text": "Between 1991 and 2000, the city was officially known as Santa Fe de Bogotá, before reverting to its original name, Bogotá.",
      "date": "1991"
    }
  ]
}

