      "text": "In 499 CE, Aryabhata composed the Āryabhaṭīya, a seminal work on mathematics and astronomy. It covers arithmetic, algebra, plane trigonometry, and spherical trigonometry, and includes continued fractions, quadratic equations, sums-of-power series, and a table of sines.",
