      "text": "On June 5, 1989, an unidentified man, known as 'Tank Man', stood in front of a column of Type 59 tanks leaving Tiananmen Square in Beijing. The lead tank stopped, and the man climbed on top of it, engaging in a brief conversation with the soldiers inside. This act of defiance was captured on film and became an iconic image worldwide.",
      "date": "1989-06-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Recognition",
      "text": "The image and video of Tank Man became internationally recognized as a symbol of peaceful protest and resistance against oppression. It is considered one of the most iconic images of the 20th century.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
