      "text": "During his wedding feast, Samson posed a riddle to his Philistine companions, which led to a series of events that increased tensions between him and the Philistines.",
      "date": "-1080"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Samson's Feats of Strength",
      "text": "Samson performed several feats of strength, including killing a lion with his bare hands and slaying 1,000 Philistines with the jawbone of a donkey.",
      "date": "-1075"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Samson and Delilah",
      "text": "Samson fell in love with Delilah, who was bribed by the Philistines to discover the secret of his strength. This led to his eventual capture.",
      "date": "-1070"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Samson's Capture and Death",
      "text": "Samson was captured by the Philistines after Delilah revealed that his strength lay in his uncut hair. He was blinded and imprisoned, but eventually brought down the temple of Dagon, killing himself and many Philistines. This event is estimated to have occurred around the late 11th century BCE.",
      "date": "-1060"
    }
  ]
}

