      "text": "Following the Wannsee Conference, the Final Solution was implemented across German-occupied Europe. This involved the deportation of Jews to extermination camps where they were systematically murdered. The genocide resulted in the murder of 90% of Polish Jews and two-thirds of the Jewish population of Europe by the end of World War II.",
      "date": "1942"
    },
