    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Haiku as a Distinct Form",
      "text": "By the 19th century, haiku had become recognized as a distinct form of poetry, separate from the hokku, largely due to the efforts of poets like Masaoka Shiki.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Masaoka Shiki's Reforms",
      "text": "Masaoka Shiki, a Japanese poet, played a significant role in modernizing haiku in the late 19th century. He advocated for haiku to be recognized as an independent poetic form.",
      "date": "1890"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Haiku to the West",
      "text": "Haiku was introduced to the Western world in the early 20th century, where it gained popularity and influenced Western poets.",
      "date": "1900"
    },
