      "text": "The 2016 United States presidential election in Michigan was held on Tuesday, November 8, 2016. Michigan voters participated in the national election to choose electors for the Electoral College. The main candidates were Republican nominee Donald Trump with running mate Mike Pence, and Democratic nominee Hillary Clinton with running mate Tim Kaine. Michigan had 16 electoral votes at stake.",
