      "headline": "Introduction of Raptor Lake",
      "text": "Raptor Lake is Intel's codename for the 13th and 14th generations of Intel Core processors. It is based on a hybrid architecture utilizing Raptor Cove performance cores and Gracemont efficient cores.",
      "date": "2022"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fabrication Process",
      "text": "Raptor Lake is fabricated using Intel's Intel 7 process, similar to its predecessor, Alder Lake.",
      "date": "2022"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Core and Thread Configuration",
      "text": "Raptor Lake features up to 24 cores and 32 threads, providing significant performance improvements over previous generations.",
      "date": "2022"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Socket Compatibility",
      "text": "Raptor Lake processors are socket compatible with Alder Lake systems, allowing for easier upgrades.",
      "date": "2022"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Issues with Elevated Voltage",
      "text": "Raptor Lake CPUs experienced issues with permanent damage from elevated voltage due to a vulnerable clock tree circuit, resulting in instability.",
      "date": "2022"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Microcode Patches Released",
      "text": "Intel released microcode patches to address the issues with elevated voltage, requiring users to update their motherboard's BIOS.",
      "date": "2022"
    }
  ]
}

