    },
    {
      "headline": "Chaucer's First Major Literary Work",
      "text": "Around 1374, Chaucer began writing 'The Book of the Duchess', his first major literary work, which was an elegy for Blanche of Lancaster.",
      "date": "1374"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appointment as Comptroller of Customs",
      "text": "In 1374, Chaucer was appointed Comptroller of Customs for the Port of London, a position he held for 12 years.",
