    },
    {
      "headline": "Education at Clergy Daughters' School",
      "text": "In 1824, Charlotte Brontë, along with her sisters, was sent to the Clergy Daughters' School at Cowan Bridge. The harsh conditions at the school later inspired the depiction of Lowood School in her novel Jane Eyre.",
      "date": "1824"
