      "headline": "Release of 'Double Indemnity'",
      "text": "In 1944, 'Double Indemnity', directed by Billy Wilder, was released. It is considered a quintessential film noir, featuring themes of crime, betrayal, and moral ambiguity.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'The Big Sleep'",
      "text": "In 1946, 'The Big Sleep', directed by Howard Hawks and starring Humphrey Bogart and Lauren Bacall, was released. It became a classic example of film noir.",
      "date": "1946"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Classic Film Noir Era",
      "text": "The classic film noir era is generally considered to have ended by the late 1950s, as the style and themes evolved and new cinematic trends emerged.",
      "date": "1959"
    },
