      "text": "Following the fire, investigations were launched to determine the cause and responsibility. Several people, including the nightclub owner Omar Chabán, were arrested in connection with the incident.",
      "date": "2005"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trial and Convictions",
      "text": "In 2009, the trial concluded with several convictions. Omar Chabán was sentenced to 20 years in prison for his role in the tragedy. Other individuals, including band members and city officials, were also convicted.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appeals and Sentence Reductions",
      "text": "In 2012, the Argentine Supreme Court upheld the convictions but reduced some sentences. Omar Chabán's sentence was reduced to 10 years and 9 months.",
      "date": "2012"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Omar Chabán",
      "text": "Omar Chabán, the owner of the República Cromañón nightclub, died of cancer on 2014-11-17 while serving his sentence.",
