      "text": "Henrietta Lacks died on October 4, 1951, at the age of 31, due to complications from cervical cancer.",
      "date": "1951-10-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of HeLa Cells",
      "text": "After her death, cells taken from Henrietta Lacks's tumor were found to be the first human cells to survive and multiply indefinitely in a laboratory setting. These cells were named HeLa cells.",
