      "text": "On December 7, 1941, Japan launched a surprise military strike on the United States naval base at Pearl Harbor, Hawaii, leading to the United States' entry into World War II.",
      "date": "1941-12-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bataan Death March",
      "text": "In April 1942, following the Battle of Bataan in the Philippines, approximately 60,000–80,000 Filipino and American prisoners of war were forced to march 65 miles under brutal conditions by the Japanese army.",
      "date": "1942-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Comfort Women System",
      "text": "Throughout the 1930s and 1940s, the Japanese military forced women from occupied territories into sexual slavery, euphemistically known as 'comfort women'.",
