      "text": "In 1986, the electoral system for the National Assembly was changed to proportional representation for that year's legislative elections, but it was reverted back to a two-round system in 1988.",
      "date": "1986"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Co-habitation Periods",
      "text": "The National Assembly has experienced several periods of co-habitation, where the President and the majority of the Assembly are from opposing parties. Notable periods include 1986-1988, 1993-1995, and 1997-2002.",
      "date": "1986"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reduction of Presidential Term",
      "text": "In 2000, a referendum resulted in the reduction of the presidential term from seven to five years, aligning it more closely with the National Assembly's term and reducing the likelihood of co-habitation.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
