      "headline": "Co-founding the Social Democracy of the Kingdom of Poland and Lithuania",
      "text": "In 1893, Rosa Luxemburg co-founded the Social Democracy of the Kingdom of Poland and Lithuania (SDKPiL), a Marxist revolutionary party.",
      "date": "1893"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Move to Germany",
      "text": "In 1898, Luxemburg moved to Germany and joined the Social Democratic Party of Germany (SPD).",
      "date": "1898"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Reform or Revolution'",
      "text": "In 1899, Luxemburg published her famous pamphlet 'Reform or Revolution', criticizing the revisionist approach within the socialist movement.",
      "date": "1899"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Involvement in the 1905 Russian Revolution",
      "text": "Rosa Luxemburg participated in the 1905 Russian Revolution, advocating for mass strikes as a means of revolutionary action.",
      "date": "1905"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Imprisonment for Anti-War Activities",
      "text": "During World War I, Luxemburg was imprisoned several times for her anti-war activities and opposition to the SPD's support for the war.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of the Spartacus League",
      "text": "In 1916, Luxemburg co-founded the Spartacus League, a revolutionary socialist organization that opposed the war and called for a proletarian revolution.",
      "date": "1916"
    },
    {
      "headline": "German Revolution and Spartacist Uprising",
      "text": "In January 1919, Luxemburg played a key role in the Spartacist Uprising in Berlin, which aimed to establish a socialist government in Germany.",
      "date": "1919-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Assassination of Rosa Luxemburg",
      "text": "On January 15, 1919, Rosa Luxemburg was captured and murdered by members of the Freikorps, a right-wing paramilitary group, in Berlin.",
      "date": "1919-01-15"
    }
  ]
}

