      "text": "The Baltic states of Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania were formed as independent countries following the end of World War I and the collapse of the Russian Empire. Estonia declared independence on February 24, 1918, Latvia on November 18, 1918, and Lithuania on February 16, 1918.",
