      "headline": "Great Fire of Meireki",
      "text": "The Great Fire of Meireki occurred in 1657, destroying much of the city and leading to significant rebuilding efforts.",
      "date": "1657"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Population Growth",
      "text": "By the early 18th century, Edo had grown to become one of the largest cities in the world, with a population of over one million.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Tokugawa Shogunate",
      "text": "The Tokugawa shogunate ended in 1868, leading to the Meiji Restoration and the renaming of Edo to Tokyo.",
      "date": "1868"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Edo Renamed Tokyo",
      "text": "In 1868, following the Meiji Restoration, Edo was renamed Tokyo, meaning 'Eastern Capital'.",
