      "headline": "Foundation of the Teutonic Order",
      "text": "The Teutonic Order was founded around 1190 in Acre, Kingdom of Jerusalem, as a Catholic religious institution and military society. It was established to aid Christians on their pilgrimages to the Holy Land and to establish hospitals.",
      "date": "1190"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Papal Recognition",
      "text": "In 1198, the Teutonic Order received papal recognition from Pope Innocent III, officially becoming a military order.",
