      "headline": "Formation of the Tajik SSR",
      "text": "The Tajik Soviet Socialist Republic was established in 1929, separating from the Uzbek SSR.",
      "date": "1929"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Kazakh and Kyrgyz SSRs",
      "text": "In 1936, the Kazakh and Kyrgyz Soviet Socialist Republics were established, upgrading from their previous status as autonomous republics within the Russian SFSR.",
      "date": "1936"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Incorporation of the Baltic States",
      "text": "In 1940, the Baltic states of Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania were incorporated into the Soviet Union as Soviet Socialist Republics.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Moldavian SSR",
      "text": "The Moldavian Soviet Socialist Republic was formed in 1940, following the annexation of Bessarabia and Northern Bukovina from Romania.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dissolution of the Transcaucasian SFSR",
      "text": "In 1936, the Transcaucasian Socialist Federative Soviet Republic was dissolved, and its territories were reorganized into the Georgian, Armenian, and Azerbaijani SSRs.",
      "date": "1936"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dissolution of the Soviet Union",
      "text": "On December 26, 1991, the Soviet Union was officially dissolved, leading to the independence of its constituent republics.",
