      "text": "The 1948 Summer Olympics were the first to be held after World War II, as the 1940 and 1944 Games were cancelled due to the war. The 1940 Games had been scheduled for Tokyo and then Helsinki, while the 1944 Games had been provisionally planned for London.",
      "date": "1948"
    },
    {
      "headline": "London hosts the Olympics for the second time",
      "text": "London became the second city to host the Summer Olympics twice, having previously hosted the Games in 1908. The 1948 Games were held from 29 July to 14 August 1948.",
      "date": "1948"
    },
