      "headline": "Development of Ska",
      "text": "Ska was developed in Jamaica in the 1960s when musicians like Stranger Cole, Prince Buster, Clement 'Coxsone' Dodd, and Duke Reid formed sound systems to play American rhythm and blues and began recording their own songs.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ska Becomes Dominant Genre",
      "text": "In the early 1960s, ska became the dominant music genre of Jamaica. It was characterized by a walking bass line accented with rhythms on the off beat.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Popularity with British Mods and Skinheads",
      "text": "In the early 1960s, ska also became popular with British mods and with many skinheads, contributing to its international spread.",
