      "headline": "Operation Barbarossa",
      "text": "The T-34 first saw combat during Operation Barbarossa, the German invasion of the Soviet Union, which began on June 22, 1941. Its performance impressed German commanders.",
      "date": "1941-06-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Moscow",
      "text": "The T-34 played a crucial role in the defense of Moscow during the winter of 1941-1942, helping to halt the German advance.",
      "date": "1941-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Stalingrad",
      "text": "The T-34 was instrumental in the Soviet victory at the Battle of Stalingrad, which lasted from August 23, 1942, to February 2, 1943.",
      "date": "1942-08-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of T-34-85",
      "text": "In response to improved German tanks, the T-34-85 was introduced in 1944, featuring an 85 mm gun and a three-man turret.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of World War II",
      "text": "The T-34 continued to be a mainstay of Soviet armored forces until the end of World War II in 1945.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-War Use",
      "text": "After World War II, the T-34 was used by various countries and saw action in numerous conflicts, including the Korean War and the Arab-Israeli wars.",
      "date": "1950"
