      "headline": "Independence and Renaming",
      "text": "On June 30, 1960, the Democratic Republic of the Congo gained independence from Belgium, with Léopoldville as its capital. The city was renamed Kinshasa on June 30, 1966.",
      "date": "1966-06-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mobutu's Regime",
      "text": "During the regime of Mobutu Sese Seko, from 1965 to 1997, Kinshasa saw significant political and economic changes, including the nationalization of industries.",
