    {
      "headline": "Emergence of Tantra",
      "text": "Tantra began to emerge as a distinct tradition in the Indian subcontinent around the middle of the 1st millennium CE. It developed within both Hinduism and Buddhism, incorporating esoteric practices and rituals.",
      "date": "0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Tantric Texts",
      "text": "Between the 6th and 13th centuries, a large body of Tantric texts was composed, including the Tantras, Agamas, and Samhitas, which outlined rituals, philosophy, and practices.",
      "date": "0600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spread of Tantra in Buddhism",
      "text": "By the 7th century, Tantric Buddhism, also known as Vajrayana, began to spread in regions such as Tibet, Nepal, and Southeast Asia, influencing local religious practices.",
      "date": "0700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Integration into Hindu Traditions",
      "text": "During the 8th to 12th centuries, Tantric practices were integrated into various Hindu traditions, including Shaivism, Shaktism, and Vaishnavism, influencing temple rituals and spiritual practices.",
      "date": "0800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peak of Tantric Influence",
      "text": "Tantra reached its peak influence between the 9th and 13th centuries, with widespread practice and the establishment of Tantric schools and lineages across the Indian subcontinent.",
      "date": "0900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline and Transformation",
      "text": "From the 13th century onwards, Tantra began to decline in prominence due to various factors, including the rise of Bhakti movements and Islamic invasions. However, it continued to transform and influence various spiritual practices.",
      "date": "1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Revival and Interest",
      "text": "In the 20th and 21st centuries, there has been a revival of interest in Tantra, both in India and globally, with scholars and practitioners exploring its spiritual, psychological, and cultural dimensions.",
      "date": "1900"
    }
  ]
}

