      "text": "In the 1890s, significant gold discoveries in places like Coolgardie and Kalgoorlie sparked a gold rush, leading to rapid population growth and economic development.",
      "date": "1890"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Federation of Australia",
      "text": "On 1 January 1901, Western Australia became a state of the newly formed Commonwealth of Australia.",
      "date": "1901-01-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Secession Referendum",
      "text": "In 1933, Western Australia held a referendum in which a majority voted to secede from the Commonwealth of Australia, but the British Parliament refused to act on the request.",
      "date": "1933"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Iron Ore Mining Boom",
      "text": "In the 1960s, the discovery of large iron ore deposits in the Pilbara region led to a mining boom that significantly boosted the state's economy.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
