      "headline": "Hijra to Medina",
      "text": "In 622 CE, Muhammad and his followers migrated from Mecca to Medina, an event known as the Hijra, marking the beginning of the Islamic calendar.",
      "date": "0622"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Badr",
      "text": "In 624 CE, the Muslims won a significant victory against the Quraysh of Mecca at the Battle of Badr.",
      "date": "0624"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conquest of Mecca",
      "text": "In 630 CE, Muhammad and his followers conquered Mecca, leading to the widespread acceptance of Islam in the Arabian Peninsula.",
      "date": "0630"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Muhammad",
      "text": "Muhammad passed away in 632 CE in Medina, leading to the succession of the first caliph, Abu Bakr.",
      "date": "0632"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Caliphate: Abu Bakr",
      "text": "Abu Bakr became the first caliph in 632 CE, initiating the Rashidun Caliphate.",
      "date": "0632"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Yarmouk",
      "text": "In 636 CE, the Muslim forces defeated the Byzantine Empire at the Battle of Yarmouk, leading to the Muslim conquest of the Levant.",
      "date": "0636"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Qadisiyyah",
      "text": "In 636 CE, the Muslim forces defeated the Sassanian Empire at the Battle of Qadisiyyah, leading to the conquest of Persia.",
      "date": "0636"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Umayyad Caliphate Established",
      "text": "In 661 CE, the Umayyad Caliphate was established by Muawiya I, marking the beginning of the Umayyad dynasty.",
      "date": "0661"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Karbala",
      "text": "In 680 CE, the Battle of Karbala took place, resulting in the martyrdom of Husayn ibn Ali and deepening the Sunni-Shia divide.",
      "date": "0680"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abbasid Caliphate Established",
      "text": "In 750 CE, the Abbasid Caliphate was established after overthrowing the Umayyad Caliphate, marking a new era in Islamic history.",
      "date": "0750"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Golden Age of Islam",
      "text": "During the 8th to 13th centuries, the Islamic world experienced a Golden Age, marked by advancements in science, technology, medicine, and culture.",
      "date": "0800"
