      "text": "Hahnemann introduced the concept of homeopathic dilution, a process where substances are repeatedly diluted and shaken, in the early 19th century.",
      "date": "1810"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the First Homeopathic School",
      "text": "In 1832, the first homeopathic school was established in Leipzig, Germany, further promoting the practice of homeopathy.",
      "date": "1832"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Homeopathy Gains Popularity in the United States",
      "text": "Homeopathy gained popularity in the United States during the mid-19th century, with the establishment of several homeopathic medical schools.",
      "date": "1850"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of Homeopathy in the 20th Century",
      "text": "During the 20th century, homeopathy began to decline in popularity due to the rise of conventional medicine and scientific skepticism.",
      "date": "1900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Resurgence of Homeopathy",
      "text": "In the late 20th and early 21st centuries, homeopathy experienced a resurgence, particularly in Europe and India, despite ongoing scientific criticism.",
      "date": "1980"
