      "text": "Proxima Centauri was discovered in 1915 by Scottish astronomer Robert Innes. It is the nearest known star to the Sun, located 4.25 light-years away in the southern constellation of Centaurus.",
      "date": "1915"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Identification as Part of Alpha Centauri System",
      "text": "Proxima Centauri is identified as component Alpha Centauri C, a member of the Alpha Centauri star system. It is 2.18° to the southwest of the Alpha Centauri AB pair.",
      "date": "1915"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Orbital Characteristics",
      "text": "Proxima Centauri is currently 12,950 AU (0.2 light-years) from the Alpha Centauri AB pair, which it orbits with a period of about 550,000 years.",
      "date": "1915"
    }
  ]
}

