      "text": "In 1923, Sigmund Freud introduced the structural model of the psyche, which included the concepts of the id, ego, and superego. This model was developed to describe the basic structure and various phenomena of mental life as encountered in psychoanalytic practice.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Ego and the Id'",
      "text": "In 1923, Freud published 'The Ego and the Id', where he elaborated on the structural model of the psyche. This work detailed the functions and interactions of the id, ego, and superego.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Translation and Adoption of Terms",
      "text": "The original German terms das Es, Ich, and Über-Ich were translated into Latin as id, ego, and superego by Freud's original translators. These terms have remained in use since their introduction.",
      "date": "1923"
    }
  ]
}

