      "text": "In 1919, Michael Collins was elected as the Minister for Finance in the First Dáil, the revolutionary parliament of the self-declared Irish Republic.",
      "date": "1919"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Anglo-Irish Treaty Negotiations",
      "text": "Michael Collins was a key figure in the negotiations of the Anglo-Irish Treaty, which were concluded on December 6, 1921. The treaty led to the establishment of the Irish Free State.",
      "date": "1921-12-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Chairman of the Provisional Government",
      "text": "On January 16, 1922, Michael Collins became the Chairman of the Provisional Government of the Irish Free State.",
      "date": "1922-01-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Commander-in-Chief of the National Army",
      "text": "In July 1922, Michael Collins was appointed as the Commander-in-Chief of the National Army during the Irish Civil War.",
      "date": "1922-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Michael Collins",
      "text": "Michael Collins was killed in an ambush on August 22, 1922, at Béal na Bláth, County Cork, during the Irish Civil War.",
      "date": "1922-08-22"
    }
  ]
}

