      "headline": "Formation of the 75th Ranger Regiment",
      "text": "The 75th Ranger Regiment was officially activated on February 3, 1986, at Fort Benning, Georgia. It was formed to provide the United States Army with a premier light infantry and direct-action raid force.",
      "date": "1986-02-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Just Cause",
      "text": "In December 1989, the 75th Ranger Regiment participated in Operation Just Cause in Panama. The Rangers were tasked with seizing the Torrijos-Tocumen Airport and other key objectives.",
      "date": "1989-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Desert Storm",
      "text": "During the Gulf War in 1991, elements of the 75th Ranger Regiment were deployed to Saudi Arabia and participated in combat operations as part of Operation Desert Storm.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Gothic Serpent",
      "text": "In 1993, the 75th Ranger Regiment was involved in Operation Gothic Serpent in Somalia, which included the Battle of Mogadishu, famously depicted in the book and film 'Black Hawk Down'.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Enduring Freedom",
      "text": "Following the September 11 attacks in 2001, the 75th Ranger Regiment was deployed to Afghanistan as part of Operation Enduring Freedom, conducting numerous combat operations against Taliban and al-Qaeda forces.",
      "date": "2001"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Iraqi Freedom",
      "text": "In 2003, the 75th Ranger Regiment participated in the invasion of Iraq, known as Operation Iraqi Freedom, conducting raids and special operations missions throughout the conflict.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion of the Regiment",
      "text": "In 2006, the 75th Ranger Regiment expanded with the activation of the Regimental Special Troops Battalion, which included the Regimental Reconnaissance Company, further enhancing its capabilities.",
      "date": "2006"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Neptune Spear",
      "text": "In May 2011, elements of the 75th Ranger Regiment were involved in Operation Neptune Spear, the mission that led to the death of Osama bin Laden in Abbottabad, Pakistan.",
      "date": "2011-05"
    }
  ]
}

