      "headline": "Formation of Blind Faith",
      "text": "In 1969, Ginger Baker formed the band Blind Faith with Eric Clapton, Steve Winwood, and Ric Grech. The band released one album and performed a tour before disbanding.",
      "date": "1969"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ginger Baker's Air Force",
      "text": "In 1970, Baker formed Ginger Baker's Air Force, a jazz-rock fusion band that included several former members of Blind Faith and other musicians.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Move to Nigeria",
      "text": "In 1971, Ginger Baker moved to Nigeria, where he collaborated with Fela Kuti and opened a recording studio in Lagos.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to the UK",
      "text": "Baker returned to the UK in the late 1970s after spending several years in Nigeria.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cream Reunion",
      "text": "In May 2005, Cream reunited for a series of concerts at the Royal Albert Hall in London, marking their first performance together in 37 years.",
      "date": "2005-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Ginger Baker",
      "text": "Ginger Baker passed away on October 6, 2019, at the age of 80, in Canterbury, Kent, England.",
