      "headline": "Construction of the World Trade Center Begins",
      "text": "Construction of the World Trade Center complex began in August 1966. The complex was designed by architect Minoru Yamasaki and developed by the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey.",
      "date": "1966-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World Trade Center Officially Opens",
      "text": "The World Trade Center was officially opened on April 4, 1973. The Twin Towers were the tallest buildings in the world at the time of their completion.",
      "date": "1973-04-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1993 World Trade Center Bombing",
      "text": "On February 26, 1993, a truck bomb exploded in the parking garage beneath the North Tower of the World Trade Center, killing six people and injuring over a thousand.",
      "date": "1993-02-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "September 11 Attacks",
      "text": "On September 11, 2001, two commercial airliners hijacked by al-Qaeda terrorists were flown into the North and South Towers of the World Trade Center. The impact and subsequent fires caused both towers to collapse, resulting in the deaths of nearly 3,000 people.",
      "date": "2001-09-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Collapse of the North Tower",
      "text": "The North Tower of the World Trade Center collapsed at 10:28 AM on September 11, 2001, 102 minutes after being struck by American Airlines Flight 11.",
      "date": "2001-09-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Collapse of the South Tower",
      "text": "The South Tower of the World Trade Center collapsed at 9:59 AM on September 11, 2001, 56 minutes after being struck by United Airlines Flight 175.",
      "date": "2001-09-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Collapse of 7 World Trade Center",
      "text": "7 World Trade Center, a 47-story building in the World Trade Center complex, collapsed at 5:20 PM on September 11, 2001, due to fires ignited by debris from the collapse of the Twin Towers.",
      "date": "2001-09-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ground Zero Cleanup Completed",
      "text": "The cleanup and recovery efforts at Ground Zero were completed in May 2002, marking the end of the debris removal process from the World Trade Center site.",
      "date": "2002-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Opening of the National September 11 Memorial & Museum",
      "text": "The National September 11 Memorial & Museum opened to the public on September 11, 2011, on the 10th anniversary of the attacks, to honor the victims and preserve the history of the events.",
      "date": "2011-09-11"
    }
  ]
}

