      "text": "In the late 1980s, rave culture and acid house music became popular in the UK, characterized by all-night dance parties and the use of psychedelic drugs.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Second Summer of Love",
      "text": "The Second Summer of Love in 1988-1989 saw the explosion of acid house music and rave culture in the UK, leading to the widespread popularity of EDM.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rise of Trance Music",
      "text": "Trance music emerged in the early 1990s, characterized by melodic synthesizers and a tempo of 125 to 150 BPM. It gained popularity in Europe.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mainstream Success of EDM",
      "text": "In the late 1990s and early 2000s, EDM began to achieve mainstream success, with artists like Daft Punk and The Chemical Brothers gaining international recognition.",
      "date": "2000"
