      "text": "On August 16, 1960, the Treaty of Establishment was signed, which granted Cyprus independence from the United Kingdom. As part of this treaty, the UK retained sovereignty over the areas of Akrotiri and Dhekelia, establishing them as British Overseas Territories.",
      "date": "1960-08-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the Sovereign Base Areas",
      "text": "Following the Treaty of Establishment in 1960, the Sovereign Base Areas of Akrotiri and Dhekelia were officially created as British Overseas Territories, allowing the UK to maintain military bases on the island of Cyprus.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cyprus Conflict and Turkish Invasion",
      "text": "In 1974, Turkey invaded Cyprus following a Greek-backed coup. The Sovereign Base Areas of Akrotiri and Dhekelia remained under British control and were not directly involved in the conflict, serving as a neutral zone.",
      "date": "1974"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Role in Signals Intelligence",
      "text": "Throughout the late 20th century and into the 21st century, Akrotiri and Dhekelia have served as key locations for the UK's signals intelligence operations, contributing to surveillance efforts in the Mediterranean and the Middle East.",
      "date": "2000"
    }
  ]
}

