      "headline": "Emergence of Neo-noir",
      "text": "The term 'neo-noir' began to be used in the late 1970s and early 1980s to describe films that adapted the visual style and themes of 1940s and 1950s American film noir for contemporary audiences.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Chinatown'",
      "text": "Roman Polanski's 'Chinatown' (1974) is often cited as a key film in the neo-noir genre, blending classic noir elements with modern themes and a complex narrative.",
      "date": "1974"
    },
