      "headline": "Release of 'Taxi Driver'",
      "text": "Martin Scorsese's 'Taxi Driver' (1976) is another seminal film in the neo-noir genre, known for its gritty portrayal of urban life and psychological depth.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Popularity Surge in the 1980s",
      "text": "During the late 1970s and early 1980s, the term 'neo-noir' surged in popularity, fueled by movies such as Sydney Pollack's 'Absence of Malice' (1981), Brian De Palma's 'Blow Out' (1981), and Martin Scorsese's 'After Hours' (1985).",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Blade Runner'",
      "text": "Ridley Scott's 'Blade Runner' (1982) is a landmark neo-noir film that combines science fiction with noir elements, influencing the genre significantly.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Blue Velvet'",
