      "headline": "Development of the Fahrenheit Scale",
      "text": "In 1724, Daniel Gabriel Fahrenheit proposed the Fahrenheit temperature scale. He defined the lower point, 0 °F, as the freezing temperature of a brine solution made from water, ice, and ammonium chloride. The upper limit was initially set at 90 °F, representing the average human body temperature, which was later adjusted to 96 °F.",
