      "headline": "Start of the Easter Rising",
      "text": "The Easter Rising began on April 24, 1916, when Irish republicans launched an armed insurrection against British rule in Ireland. The aim was to establish an independent Irish Republic.",
      "date": "1916-04-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Proclamation of the Irish Republic",
      "text": "On April 24, 1916, the leaders of the Easter Rising proclaimed the establishment of the Irish Republic from the steps of the General Post Office in Dublin.",
      "date": "1916-04-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Easter Rising",
      "text": "The Easter Rising ended on April 29, 1916, after six days of fighting. The leaders of the rebellion surrendered to British forces.",
      "date": "1916-04-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Execution of Leaders",
      "text": "Starting in May 1916, sixteen leaders of the Easter Rising were executed by British authorities. The executions began on May 3, 1916, and continued until May 12, 1916.",
      "date": "1916-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Impact on Irish Independence Movement",
      "text": "The nature of the executions and subsequent political developments contributed to an increase in popular support for Irish independence, ultimately leading to the Irish War of Independence.",
      "date": "1916"
    }
  ]
}

