      "text": "Sam Houston joined the United States Army in 1813 and served under General Andrew Jackson during the War of 1812.",
      "date": "1813"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Horseshoe Bend",
      "text": "On March 27, 1814, Sam Houston was wounded at the Battle of Horseshoe Bend, a decisive battle in the Creek War.",
      "date": "1814-03-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Elected to Congress",
      "text": "In 1823, Sam Houston was elected to the United States House of Representatives from Tennessee.",
      "date": "1823"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Governor of Tennessee",
      "text": "Sam Houston became the sixth governor of Tennessee in 1827.",
      "date": "1827"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Resignation as Governor",
      "text": "In 1829, Sam Houston resigned as governor of Tennessee following a scandal involving his marriage.",
      "date": "1829"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Move to Texas",
      "text": "In 1832, Sam Houston moved to Texas, which was then part of Mexico.",
      "date": "1832"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Commander-in-Chief of Texan Army",
      "text": "In 1835, Sam Houston was appointed Commander-in-Chief of the Texan Army during the Texas Revolution.",
      "date": "1835"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Victory at the Battle of San Jacinto",
      "text": "On April 21, 1836, Sam Houston led Texan forces to victory against the Mexican army at the Battle of San Jacinto, securing Texas independence.",
      "date": "1836-04-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First President of the Republic of Texas",
      "text": "Sam Houston was elected as the first President of the Republic of Texas in 1836.",
      "date": "1836"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Term as President of Texas",
      "text": "Sam Houston served a second term as President of the Republic of Texas from 1841 to 1844.",
      "date": "1841"
    },
    {
      "headline": "U.S. Senator from Texas",
      "text": "In 1846, Sam Houston became one of the first two senators to represent Texas in the United States Senate.",
      "date": "1846"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Governor of Texas",
      "text": "Sam Houston was elected as the seventh governor of Texas in 1859.",
      "date": "1859"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Removal from Office",
      "text": "In 1861, Sam Houston was removed from office as governor of Texas for refusing to swear loyalty to the Confederacy.",
      "date": "1861"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Sam Houston",
      "text": "Sam Houston died on July 26, 1863, in Huntsville, Texas.",
