      "text": "The Statue of Zeus at Olympia was constructed by the Greek sculptor Phidias around 435 BCE. It was a giant seated figure, approximately 12.4 meters (41 feet) tall, and was erected in the Temple of Zeus at the sanctuary of Olympia, Greece.",
