      "text": "The Civil Rights Act of 1866 was passed on April 9, 1866, granting citizenship and equal rights to all persons born in the United States, regardless of race.",
      "date": "1866-04-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ratification of the 14th Amendment",
      "text": "The 14th Amendment, granting citizenship to all persons born or naturalized in the United States and providing equal protection under the laws, was ratified on July 9, 1868.",
      "date": "1868-07-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Reconstruction Act",
      "text": "The First Reconstruction Act was passed on March 2, 1867, dividing the South into five military districts and outlining how new governments based on universal male suffrage were to be established.",
      "date": "1867-03-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ratification of the 15th Amendment",
      "text": "The 15th Amendment, prohibiting the federal and state governments from denying a citizen the right to vote based on race, color, or previous condition of servitude, was ratified on February 3, 1870.",
      "date": "1870-02-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Reconstruction",
      "text": "Reconstruction officially ended in 1877 with the Compromise of 1877, which resulted in the withdrawal of federal troops from the South and the end of federal efforts to protect the rights of African Americans.",
