    },
    {
      "headline": "Efforts to Control the Fire",
      "text": "On 4 September 1666, efforts to control the fire included creating firebreaks by demolishing buildings, but these were largely unsuccessful due to the intensity of the flames.",
      "date": "1666-09-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fire Reaches St. Paul's Cathedral",
      "text": "On 4 September 1666, the fire reached St. Paul's Cathedral, which was completely destroyed.",
      "date": "1666-09-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fire Brought Under Control",
      "text": "By 5 September 1666, the winds had died down, and the fire was gradually brought under control.",
      "date": "1666-09-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Great Fire",
      "text": "The Great Fire of London was finally extinguished on Thursday, 6 September 1666.",
      "date": "1666-09-06"
    },
